id: jf-36oy
title: Enforce structured output formats across dedicated Jellyfin commands
description: "Replace TOON-only command output paths with the shared typed formatter so every advertised format remains syntactically valid and schema-consistent across read and mutation command families, while preserving TOON as the default."
type: Plan
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[11]: agents,api,formats,json,markdown,quality,raw,read-only,table,toon,yaml
created_at: "2026-08-05T20:20:16.290Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-05T21:29:49.670Z"
assignee: codex-jellyfin-format-20260805
author: codex-jellyfin-format-20260805
estimated_minutes: 900
acceptance_criteria: Every leaf command that advertises or inherits format selection honors toon json yaml markdown table and raw through one typed output boundary; TOON remains the default and preserves existing normalized envelopes; JSON stdout parses for every covered command and formatter schemas round-trip; mutation commands are tested only against isolated fixtures and live Jellyfin testing remains read-only; help and documentation describe exact output behavior; release validation PM validation security privacy review and auto-release readiness gates pass
definition_of_ready: All 46 PM items and histories inspected at project/relevant-detail level; all-status duplicate and graph audits clean; latest pm-cli and pm-changelog verified; clean main; official release and live server both 10.11.11; defect reproduced without exposing private data.
goal: jf-mqpo
value: "Make jf-cli dependable in jq, CI, YAML, Markdown, and agent pipelines instead of silently returning the wrong serialization."
impact: Removes a repo-wide automation footgun across hundreds of dedicated Jellyfin commands and all supported output consumers.
outcome: A single enforceable structured-output contract across the complete dedicated command surface with read-only live proof.
why_now: "The newest API coverage tranche proved endpoint reach, but direct live probes show the dedicated interface still violates its advertised serialization contract."
parent: jf-gn5j
reviewer: github-review-bots
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: jellyfin-10.11.11
release: next-manual-release
